  "question": {
    "text": "The foot of perpendicular from the origin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> to a plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> which meets the co-ordinate axes at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi></math>. If the volume of the tetrahedron <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>144</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>unit</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, then which of the following points is NOT on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Plotting the diagram of the given data we get,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0136_5b07f364c57a.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 230px;\" /></p><p>As&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;the foot of perpendicular from origin,</p><p>So, direction ratio of normal vector will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>So, equation of plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Now Volume of tetrahedron&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>C</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>144</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></math></p><p>Let&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>k</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>So, equation of plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p>Clearly all three points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math> satisfy&nbsp;the equation of plane but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math> does not satisfy plane</p>"
  }
}